# What never belongs in the repository.
#
# Grouped by why, because a list of forty lines with no reason attached is a list
# nobody edits: the next person adds a duplicate rather than work out what is already
# covered.

# Dependencies. pnpm keeps a store of its own and links from it.
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
*.tgz

# What a build produces. Every one of these is written again by pnpm build. Build and
# out are anchored at the root: unanchored they hid any folder of that name, a source
# folder included.
dist/
/build/
/out/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Caches of the tools. Turborepo, Vite and Biome all keep one, and none of them is
# worth sharing: they are keyed to the machine that wrote them.
.turbo/
.cache/
.eslintcache

# Secrets. The example is the only one that travels, and it holds no real value.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars*

# Databases. In browser mode the database is inside the browser, and on a server it is
# a file. Neither is ever committed, and a stray one in a working copy is somebody's
# real money.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Where a server keeps its file when nothing says otherwise, and a folder of that name at
# the root. Unanchored, this hid every folder called data, source folders included.
/data/
apps/server/data/

# What the test runners leave behind.
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/
blob-report/

# Throwaway pictures and reports taken for a review, wherever the camera ran from. A
# folder only, so the spec that takes them, shots.spec.ts, is never caught.
shots/

# Real documents read by the statement reader while it is being taught an institution.
# The content and never the folder, or the README could not come back in.
**/samples/*
!/samples/README.md

# What a bank hands over and what this application writes out, when it lands at the root
# of the clone: statements, spreadsheets, backups and dumps. At the root only, because a
# rule everywhere would hide a template kept in apps/web/public. Anywhere else, the check
# in scripts/checkRepository.mjs is what refuses them.
/*.pdf
/*.ofx
/*.qfx
/*.qif
/*.csv
/*.xls
/*.xlsx
/*.json.gz
/cofre_*.json
/*.tar.gz
/*.sql

# Logs.
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*

# Hosts that write into the working copy.
.vercel/
.netlify/
.wrangler/

# Notes to the tooling, not to the product.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/

# Editors and operating systems.
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
